From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:50:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Describe stored held marks, stale offer cards and the
 reload rule in the docs

QUIRKS.md (Fix round 6, log): the restart rule flipped, held marks on the
Lightkeeper's copy, a held mark kept over a reload, with their tests.
WEBSOCKET.md: the desk's persisted marks. DESIGN.md: held boxes on the
Lightkeeper's copy and the reload notice. FAQ.md: what a restart and a
reload keep.

Checked in Chromium at 390x844, 820x1180 and 1366x768: the Lightkeeper's
copy draws a held Body mark live and fills it when declined; a mark taken
in a stalled socket comes back after a reload and is taken once, and a
stale one is let go with the notice; after a backend restart the desk gets
the same offer and log, and a card whose offer was not stored closes on
Take the mark with nothing landed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
