 **The creator's action ratings** (step 3, playtest 2026-10-10) draw a point the specialty gave as a faded pip in a sepia ring and the player's own points (the free raise and the three free points) as full pips. Each action's gild sits beside its name: an open sepia star where the free gild may go, the star on a gold disc in a sepia ring once gilded, and on the specialty's gild, which is fixed, a small ink padlock as well. Every gilded action shows the disc whatever its rating (an action at 0 has no pip to gild), so the two gilds always look alike but for the padlock. Under part B's heading a line of its own, "Gild One More Action" with the open star and its "choose one" (the action's name with a tick once chosen), then "Key to the marks" with its "i" (`InfoTerm`), whose slip shows the marks on hover, focus or a tap: From your specialty, Your points, Gilded, Gilded by your specialty. Nothing of the key is printed on the page. The foot of the step reads "Gilded: Focus (your specialty), Sway", marking the specialty's action in place; its locked padlock star's `title` reads "Gilded by your specialty".
 
