--- a/FAQ.md
+++ b/FAQ.md
@@ -113,6 +113,8 @@ Characters have three mark tracks: **Body**, **Brain**, and **Bleed** (0–3 eac
 
 If none of these apply (or the player declines), the mark is applied and the character sheet is updated in real time.
 
+A mark held for a soak or Death Defy is stored with its offer, so a server restart (a deploy) keeps it: the desk gets the same offer again when it reconnects, and the Lightkeeper's copy of the sheet draws it held. An answer to an offer the server no longer holds lands nothing, and the card closes. The allies' offers (Behind Me, Premonitions, Non-Combatant's drive point) and Adrenaline Rush are not stored: after a restart they are gone, and an answer to one is refused as too late. A mark sent from the sheet and not yet answered is kept by the browser over a reload and sent again once the desk reconnects, taken once; one taken more than ten minutes before the reload is let go with a note under the marks. The Activity Log is stored too (each campaign's last 500 lines), so a restart empties no desk's log.
+
 Since 2026-10-10 every mark that lands this way, taken on the player's own sheet or dealt by the Lightkeeper, writes one line in the Activity Log on every desk with the track's count ("Dr. Imogen Thale took a Body mark (1 of 3)."; a mark the Lightkeeper dealt that lands at once reads "The Lightkeeper dealt Dr. Imogen Thale a Body mark (1 of 3)."), and names the offer the player let go: "passed on Death Defy and took a Bleed mark (1 of 3)." when they pressed "Take the mark", "let Death Defy run out and took a Bleed mark (1 of 3)." when its countdown ran out. A mark an ability takes as its cost (Ritual, Occult Researcher, Back Against the Wall, Bending Spoons) is named in that ability's own line instead, so it is not logged twice.
 
 ### What happens on the 4th mark?
