 Issues #17, #18, #23 and #43, built to decision 1 of fix round 6 (restarts lose nothing a player can see). The pinned expectations were flipped, not deleted.
 
 - The Activity Log lived in the server's memory (#17), so a restart (every deploy) emptied every desk's log. A campaign's lines are stored (table activity_lines, the campaign's last 500), and a desk that opens gets its last 100 as before, after a restart too. Lines of a socket with no campaign still live in memory. Tests: test_ws_connect.test_the_log_survives_a_restart, test_a_campaign_keeps_its_last_lines, test_the_history_keeps_each_campaigns_lines_apart and test_the_history_keeps_the_newest_lines (now on real campaigns); test_ws_rolls' secret-line tests read the stored lines.
+- A held mark (soak, Circle of Protection, Death Defy) lived in the server's memory (#17), and so did the ids of the marks a desk sent: a restart lost the mark, and the card's decline then landed it by the restart rule (#18), the pinned behaviour. The held mark is stored with its offer and offer_id (characters.held_mark) and comes back on connect with the same id; the mark ids too (characters.taken_mark_ids, the last 16). An answer naming an offer the server does not hold lands nothing and gets mark_offer_closed with dropped and that offer_id, which closes only that card. Behind Me, Premonitions, Adrenaline Rush and Non-Combatant still live in memory, on purpose (decision 1): after a restart they are gone and an answer gets the existing refusal. Tests: test_an_answer_from_before_a_restart_lands_no_mark (was test_an_answer_from_before_a_restart_still_lands_its_mark), test_a_held_mark_survives_a_restart, test_a_death_defy_offer_counts_on_after_a_restart, test_ally_offers_expire_cleanly_after_a_restart, test_a_mark_sent_again_after_a_restart_is_taken_once; test_a_held_mark_that_lands_early_closes_its_offer, test_an_answer_to_a_closed_offer_is_ignored and test_an_answer_to_a_death_defy_offer_counted_again_is_ignored now expect the dropped reply. The desk's side was checked in the browser.
+- The Lightkeeper's copy of a sheet did not show held marks (#23): the sheet carries held_marks {ability, mark_types}, each offer sends her the sheet, and her read-only copy draws dashed held boxes with the "held for" line. Test: test_the_lightkeepers_copy_of_the_sheet_draws_a_held_mark.
+- A mark taken during a silent outage was lost if the page was reloaded before the desk reconnected (#43): only the store in memory kept it. An unanswered mark sent from the sheet is kept in the browser (store heldMarks, persisted) with its mark_id and the time, and sent again when the same character's socket opens; the server takes it once, a restart in between included. One taken more than ten minutes before the reload is let go with "A Body mark taken before the reload may not have counted. Check the trauma record." under the marks. Checked in the browser; there is no frontend test runner.
